### Worked cost-to-evade sentence [alt-trip]
To exfiltrate the Ronin-scale 173,600 ETH while keeping the adaptive attacker's best detection probability < 50% (with distinct cash-out destinations capped at 4), the search's best evasive schedule needs 174 tx over a horizon of 87,581 s (~1.0 days), forcing the effective extraction RATE down to 1.987 ETH/s — a ~503.3x collapse from the 1,000.000 ETH/s achievable at the smallest budget. Composed through the limiter+breaker+Δ, realised on-chain extraction is pinned at <= 1,506 ETH per detection interval (D+Δ=540 s, within one breaker window W=3,600 s) — itself <= the patient Phase-14 bound B+r·D+r·Δ = 1,540 ETH, under the rate-limiter FLOOR T+r·Δ = 4,060 ETH the attacker can NEVER beat within a window. That per-interval cap is only ~0.87% of the 173,600-ETH Ronin loss: draining the full target at this cap would require >= 116 sequential detection-and-halt cycles spanning >= 62,237 s (~0.7 days), each cycle re-tripping the breaker — so no single detection window ever releases more than a tiny fraction of what Ronin lost undetected over 6 days.
#
